var e=JSON.parse(`[{"id":"MCMA-R-001","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["health","science"],"passage":"The Mediterranean diet, characterized by high consumption of fruits, vegetables, whole grains, olive oil, and moderate intake of fish and poultry, has been extensively studied for its health benefits. Research has consistently shown that populations following this dietary pattern have lower rates of cardiovascular disease, certain types of cancer, and cognitive decline in old age. The diet is rich in antioxidants and anti-inflammatory compounds, which are believed to be responsible for many of its protective effects. Additionally, the Mediterranean lifestyle includes regular physical activity and an emphasis on sharing meals with family and friends, which may also contribute to overall wellbeing.","question":"Which of the following are mentioned as benefits or characteristics of the Mediterranean diet?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Lower rates of heart disease","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Exclusive consumption of red meat","isCorrect":false},{"id":"c","text":"Rich in anti-inflammatory compounds","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Includes social aspects like sharing meals","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-002","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["technology","society"],"passage":"The adoption of renewable energy sources has accelerated dramatically in the past decade. Solar and wind power have become increasingly cost-competitive with fossil fuels, leading to their widespread deployment across both developed and developing nations. Governments have played a crucial role in this transition through subsidies, tax incentives, and regulatory frameworks that encourage clean energy investment. However, challenges remain, including the intermittent nature of solar and wind power, the need for improved energy storage technologies, and the requirement for substantial infrastructure upgrades to accommodate new energy systems.","question":"According to the passage, which factors have contributed to the growth of renewable energy?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Government subsidies and incentives","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Decreasing costs of solar and wind technology","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Complete replacement of fossil fuel infrastructure","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Regulatory support for clean energy","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-003","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["education","psychology"],"passage":"The concept of multiple intelligences, proposed by psychologist Howard Gardner in 1983, challenges the traditional view of intelligence as a single, unified ability measured by IQ tests. Gardner identified eight distinct types of intelligence, including linguistic, logical-mathematical, spatial, musical, bodily-kinesthetic, interpersonal, intrapersonal, and naturalistic. According to this theory, individuals possess varying strengths across these different domains, and educational systems should adapt their teaching methods to accommodate this diversity. Critics of the theory argue that some of Gardner's categories are better described as talents or personality traits rather than distinct forms of intelligence.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following statements are true about Gardner's theory of multiple intelligences?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It identifies eight different types of intelligence","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"It was proposed in the 1980s","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"It has been universally accepted without criticism","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Musical intelligence is one of the identified categories","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"It suggests IQ tests are the best measure of intelligence","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-004","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["environment","pollution"],"passage":"Plastic pollution has become one of the most pressing environmental issues of our time. Single-use plastics, such as bags, straws, and packaging, account for a significant portion of the waste found in oceans and waterways. Once in the environment, plastics can take hundreds of years to decompose, breaking down into smaller particles known as microplastics. These particles have been found in drinking water, seafood, and even the air we breathe. Marine animals often mistake plastic debris for food, which can lead to starvation, internal injuries, and death. Reducing plastic consumption and improving waste management infrastructure are both critical for addressing this problem.","question":"Which of the following are mentioned in the passage as aspects of the plastic pollution problem?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Microplastics have been detected in drinking water","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Plastic can take centuries to decompose in the environment","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Marine animals can mistake plastic for food","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"All plastic waste comes from industrial sources","isCorrect":false},{"id":"e","text":"Improving waste management is one solution mentioned","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-005","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["history","economics"],"passage":"The Great Depression, which began with the stock market crash of 1929, was the most severe economic downturn in modern history. Banks failed in large numbers as depositors rushed to withdraw their savings, leading to a collapse of credit availability. Industrial production fell dramatically, and unemployment rates soared to unprecedented levels, reaching approximately 25 percent in the United States. The crisis spread globally as international trade contracted and countries imposed protective tariffs. The economic devastation led to significant changes in government policy, including the establishment of social safety nets and increased financial regulation. The Depression also contributed to political instability in several countries, most notably Germany, where it facilitated the rise of extremist movements.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following occurred during or as a result of the Great Depression?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Widespread bank failures","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Unemployment reached approximately 25 percent in the US","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Increased international trade and cooperation","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Establishment of social safety nets","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Rise of extremist political movements in some countries","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-006","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["science","biology"],"passage":"The human microbiome consists of trillions of microorganisms, including bacteria, viruses, and fungi, that live in and on the human body. These microbes play essential roles in digestion, immune system development, and even mental health. The gut microbiome, in particular, has been the subject of intensive research, with studies linking its composition to conditions ranging from obesity to depression. Diet is one of the most significant factors influencing the makeup of the gut microbiome, with fiber-rich foods promoting the growth of beneficial bacteria. Antibiotic use, on the other hand, can disrupt the microbial balance and potentially lead to health complications such as antibiotic-resistant infections.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are true about the human microbiome?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It consists only of bacteria","isCorrect":false},{"id":"b","text":"Diet significantly influences gut microbiome composition","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Fiber-rich foods promote beneficial bacteria","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Antibiotics can disrupt microbial balance","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"The microbiome has no connection to mental health","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-007","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["business","management"],"passage":"Remote work has become increasingly prevalent since the global shift in workplace practices. Organizations that have embraced remote and hybrid models report several benefits, including reduced overhead costs from smaller office spaces and access to a broader talent pool unrestricted by geographic location. Employee surveys consistently show that many workers value the flexibility that remote work provides, citing improved work-life balance and elimination of commuting time. However, managers have noted challenges in maintaining team cohesion, fostering spontaneous collaboration, and ensuring consistent communication across distributed teams. Successful remote organizations typically invest in collaboration tools and establish clear expectations for availability and deliverables.","question":"Which of the following benefits or challenges of remote work are mentioned in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Reduced office overhead costs","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Access to a wider talent pool","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Elimination of all workplace problems","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Improved work-life balance for employees","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Difficulty maintaining spontaneous collaboration","isCorrect":true},{"id":"f","text":"Remote work is cheaper for employees in all cases","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-008","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["health","sleep"],"passage":"Sleep plays a vital role in maintaining physical health and cognitive function. During deep sleep stages, the body repairs tissues, builds bone and muscle, and strengthens the immune system. The brain consolidates memories from the day, transferring important information from short-term to long-term storage. Chronic sleep deprivation has been linked to a range of health problems including increased risk of heart disease, diabetes, and weakened immune response. Cognitive effects include impaired attention, slower reaction times, and reduced ability to learn new information. Most adults require seven to nine hours of sleep per night, though individual needs vary based on genetics and lifestyle factors.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are effects or functions of sleep?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Tissue repair during deep sleep","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Memory consolidation","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Increased risk of heart disease from sleep deprivation","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Sleep deprivation improving attention","isCorrect":false},{"id":"e","text":"Immune system strengthening","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-009","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["technology","ethics"],"passage":"The rapid development of artificial intelligence has generated significant debate about its societal implications. On one hand, AI systems have demonstrated remarkable capabilities in areas such as medical diagnosis, where they can sometimes detect diseases earlier than human doctors. AI-powered automation also promises to increase productivity and free workers from repetitive, mundane tasks. On the other hand, concerns have been raised about algorithmic bias, where AI systems perpetuate or amplify existing social inequalities due to biased training data. The potential for widespread job displacement in certain sectors has also prompted calls for proactive workforce retraining programs. Furthermore, questions about accountability arise when autonomous systems make mistakes, as it is not always clear who bears legal responsibility.","question":"Which of the following concerns about AI are discussed in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Algorithmic bias perpetuating social inequalities","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Potential job displacement in certain sectors","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"AI systems being too slow to process medical data","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Unclear legal accountability for autonomous system errors","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"AI completely replacing human doctors","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-010","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["education","learning"],"passage":"Bilingual education programs have been implemented in schools around the world with varying approaches. Some programs use a dual-language immersion model, where students receive instruction in two languages throughout the school day. Other models emphasize transitional bilingual education, gradually shifting from the student's native language to the dominant language of the country. Research has consistently shown that bilingualism provides cognitive benefits, including enhanced executive function, better problem-solving skills, and improved metalinguistic awareness. Additionally, bilingual individuals may have greater employment opportunities in an increasingly globalized economy. Despite these advantages, bilingual programs sometimes face resistance due to political concerns or resource limitations.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are true about bilingual education?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Dual-language immersion is one type of bilingual program","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Bilingualism can improve problem-solving skills","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"All schools use the same bilingual education model","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Bilingual individuals may have more job opportunities","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Bilingual programs never face any opposition","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-011","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["environment","climate change"],"passage":"Climate change is driving shifts in weather patterns, ecosystems, and human activities across the globe. Rising global temperatures are causing polar ice caps and glaciers to melt at accelerated rates, contributing to sea level rise that threatens coastal communities. Warmer oceans are also leading to more intense tropical storms and hurricanes, as these weather systems draw energy from warm surface waters. In agricultural regions, changing precipitation patterns and increased frequency of droughts are affecting crop yields and food security. Scientists emphasize that while some level of climate change is already unavoidable due to past emissions, immediate and substantial reductions in greenhouse gas emissions could prevent the most catastrophic scenarios.","question":"Which of the following impacts of climate change are described in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Accelerated melting of polar ice caps and glaciers","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Sea level rise threatening coastal communities","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Decreased frequency of tropical storms","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Changing precipitation patterns affecting agriculture","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Immediate emission reductions could prevent the worst outcomes","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-012","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["philosophy","politics"],"passage":"The concept of the social contract has been central to Western political philosophy since the Enlightenment period. Thomas Hobbes argued that in a state of nature, without government authority, human life would be solitary and brutal, and that individuals therefore rationally consent to surrender some freedoms in exchange for security and order. John Locke offered a more optimistic view, contending that people possess natural rights to life, liberty, and property that governments are established to protect, and that citizens have the right to revolt against tyrannical rule. Jean-Jacques Rousseau further developed the idea, emphasizing that legitimate political authority must derive from the general will of the people rather than from force or divine right. These philosophical foundations profoundly influenced the development of modern democratic institutions and constitutional frameworks.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following ideas are associated with the philosophers mentioned?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Hobbes believed life without government would be brutal","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Locke argued people have natural rights to life, liberty, and property","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Rousseau favored absolute monarchy","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Rousseau emphasized the general will of the people","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Social contract ideas influenced modern democratic institutions","isCorrect":true},{"id":"f","text":"Locke opposed the right to revolt against tyranny","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-013","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["media","advertising"],"passage":"Advertising has evolved significantly in the digital age, moving beyond traditional print and broadcast media to encompass a wide range of online platforms. Digital advertising offers advantages such as precise audience targeting, real-time performance measurement, and the ability to personalize messages for individual consumers. Social media platforms have become particularly important advertising channels, as they provide detailed user data that enables advertisers to reach specific demographic groups. However, concerns have been raised about the privacy implications of targeted advertising and the potential for manipulative marketing practices. In response, many countries have introduced data protection regulations that restrict how companies can collect and use consumer information for advertising purposes.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are characteristics of digital advertising?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Precise audience targeting capabilities","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Real-time performance measurement","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Personalized messaging for consumers","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Complete elimination of privacy concerns","isCorrect":false},{"id":"e","text":"Social media platforms provide user data for targeting","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-014","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["sports","science"],"passage":"The science of sports performance has advanced considerably, integrating knowledge from physiology, biomechanics, nutrition, and psychology. Modern training programs are highly individualized, taking into account an athlete's specific physiological profile, sport-specific demands, and injury history. Recovery has emerged as a critical component of training, with emphasis on adequate sleep, proper nutrition, and active recovery techniques such as foam rolling and light movement. Sports psychologists work with athletes to develop mental skills including goal setting, visualization, and stress management. Technology has also become integral, with wearable devices tracking metrics such as heart rate variability, sleep quality, and training load to optimize performance and reduce injury risk.","question":"Which of the following are mentioned as components of modern sports performance training?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Individualized training programs","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Recovery techniques including adequate sleep and nutrition","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Mental skills training with sports psychologists","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Use of wearable technology to track metrics","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Elimination of all rest days from training","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-015","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["history","art"],"passage":"Impressionism emerged in France during the late 19th century as a radical departure from academic painting traditions. Rather than working in studios to produce carefully finished works, Impressionist artists such as Claude Monet, Pierre-Auguste Renoir, and Edgar Degas frequently painted outdoors to capture the transient effects of natural light. Their distinctive technique involved using short, visible brushstrokes and vibrant colors applied side by side rather than blended on the palette, allowing the viewer's eye to optically mix the colors. Initially rejected by the established art world, with their works excluded from the official Salon exhibitions, the Impressionists organized their own independent shows. Over time, their innovations influenced virtually all subsequent modern art movements and Impressionism is now among the most beloved and commercially successful styles in art history.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are characteristics of Impressionism?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Painting outdoors to capture natural light","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Use of short, visible brushstrokes","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Colors applied side by side for optical mixing","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Initially rejected by the established art world","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Using exclusively blended colors on the palette","isCorrect":false},{"id":"f","text":"Influenced subsequent modern art movements","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-016","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["health","nutrition"],"passage":"Vitamin D plays a crucial role in the body, primarily in regulating calcium and phosphate levels, which are essential for maintaining healthy bones and teeth. Unlike most vitamins, the body can synthesize vitamin D when skin is exposed to sunlight, which is why it is often referred to as the sunshine vitamin. However, many people do not get adequate sun exposure, particularly in winter months or in northern latitudes, leading to widespread vitamin D insufficiency. Dietary sources include oily fish, egg yolks, and fortified foods such as milk and breakfast cereals. Severe vitamin D deficiency can lead to rickets in children and osteomalacia in adults, conditions characterized by weak and softened bones.","question":"Which of the following are true about vitamin D according to the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It helps regulate calcium and phosphate in the body","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"The body can produce it through sun exposure","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"It is found exclusively in plant-based foods","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Deficiency can cause bone conditions like rickets","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"It cannot be obtained from any dietary sources","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-017","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["technology","history"],"passage":"The development of agriculture approximately 10,000 years ago is often considered the single most important event in human history. This transition from hunting and gathering to farming allowed human populations to grow significantly, as food supplies became more reliable and capable of supporting larger communities. Settled agricultural life also led to the development of complex societies, specialization of labor, and the emergence of cities. However, the agricultural revolution also brought negative consequences, including a less diverse diet for many people, increased spread of infectious diseases due to higher population densities, and the beginnings of social inequality as some individuals accumulated more wealth and resources than others.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following were consequences of the agricultural revolution?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Growth in human population sizes","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Development of complex societies and cities","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Complete elimination of all diseases","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Increased spread of infectious diseases","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Emergence of social inequality","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-018","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["psychology","behavior"],"passage":"Habits are automatic behaviors that are triggered by contextual cues and performed with minimal conscious thought. According to research by psychologists, habits form through a three-step loop process consisting of a cue, a routine, and a reward. The cue triggers the brain to initiate a behavior, the routine is the behavior itself, and the reward helps the brain determine whether the particular loop is worth remembering. Understanding this loop has practical applications for changing unwanted habits, as individuals can learn to identify their cues and modify their routines while maintaining similar rewards. This approach has been successfully applied in areas ranging from smoking cessation to improving dietary choices.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are true about habits?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"They involve a three-step loop of cue, routine, and reward","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"They are always conscious and deliberate actions","isCorrect":false},{"id":"c","text":"Identifying cues can help in changing unwanted habits","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"The habit loop has been used to help people stop smoking","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-019","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["environment","oceans"],"passage":"Coral reefs are among the most diverse and productive ecosystems on the planet. They provide critical habitat for approximately 25 percent of all marine species while covering less than one percent of the ocean floor. Reefs also offer substantial economic benefits through fisheries, tourism, and coastal protection, with some estimates valuing these services at billions of dollars annually. However, coral reefs face multiple threats, including ocean warming, which causes coral bleaching, ocean acidification, which impairs coral growth, pollution from agricultural runoff, and destructive fishing practices. Scientists warn that without significant reductions in greenhouse gas emissions and improved local management, most of the world's coral reefs could be severely degraded by mid-century.","question":"Which of the following threats to coral reefs are mentioned in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Ocean warming causing coral bleaching","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Ocean acidification impairing coral growth","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Natural predators consuming all coral species","isCorrect":false},{"id":"d","text":"Pollution from agricultural runoff","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Destructive fishing practices","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-020","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["education","teaching methods"],"passage":"Collaborative learning is an educational approach that involves groups of students working together to solve problems, complete tasks, or understand new concepts. Research has demonstrated that this approach can improve academic achievement, enhance critical thinking skills, and develop social and communication abilities. When students explain concepts to peers, they consolidate their own understanding while helping others learn. However, successful collaborative learning requires careful structuring by teachers to ensure that all group members contribute meaningfully and that individual accountability is maintained. Group composition, task design, and clear assessment criteria all influence the effectiveness of collaborative activities.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are benefits of collaborative learning?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Improved academic achievement","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Enhanced critical thinking skills","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Development of social and communication abilities","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Complete elimination of the need for teachers","isCorrect":false},{"id":"e","text":"Consolidation of understanding when explaining to peers","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-021","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["history","politics"],"passage":"Decolonization, the process by which colonies became independent from European colonial powers, fundamentally reshaped the global political order in the decades following World War II. Several factors converged to accelerate this process, including the weakening of European powers after the war, the rise of nationalist movements in colonized territories, and pressure from the newly formed United Nations and the two emerging superpowers, the United States and the Soviet Union. India's independence from Britain in 1947 set an important precedent, and within two decades, dozens of new nations had emerged across Africa and Asia. The transition was not always peaceful, as evidenced by protracted conflicts in places such as Algeria and Vietnam. Post-colonial challenges included building stable political institutions, addressing ethnic divisions exacerbated by colonial rule, and overcoming economic underdevelopment.","question":"Which of the following are mentioned in the passage as factors contributing to decolonization?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Weakening of European powers after World War II","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Rise of nationalist movements in colonies","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Pressure from the United Nations and superpowers","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"India's independence set an important precedent","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"All transitions were entirely peaceful","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-022","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["science","astronomy"],"passage":"Mars has long captured the human imagination as a potential destination for exploration and possibly even colonization. Recent missions by NASA and other space agencies have revealed compelling evidence that liquid water once flowed on the Martian surface, and that subsurface water ice still exists in substantial quantities. The presence of organic molecules in Martian soil, detected by the Curiosity rover, has fueled speculation about the possibility of past microbial life on the planet. However, significant challenges remain for any future human mission, including the long travel time of approximately seven months, exposure to cosmic radiation, and the psychological challenges of isolation and confinement. Despite these obstacles, both government agencies and private companies are developing plans for crewed Mars missions within the next few decades.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are true about Mars exploration?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Evidence suggests liquid water once existed on Mars","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Organic molecules have been detected in Martian soil","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Human travel to Mars takes approximately seven months","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Cosmic radiation is a significant challenge for human missions","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Mars has already been successfully colonized by humans","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-023","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["business","entrepreneurship"],"passage":"Small businesses are often described as the backbone of the economy, accounting for a significant share of employment and economic output in most countries. They tend to be more flexible and adaptable than large corporations, allowing them to respond quickly to changing market conditions. Small businesses also play a crucial role in fostering innovation, as entrepreneurs often pursue ideas that larger, more established companies consider too risky or unproven. However, small businesses face considerable challenges, including difficulty accessing capital, competing against larger firms with economies of scale, and navigating complex regulatory requirements. Government programs such as small business loans and mentorship initiatives aim to address some of these obstacles.","question":"Which of the following statements about small businesses are supported by the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"They account for significant employment in most countries","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"They are generally more flexible than large corporations","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"They play an important role in fostering innovation","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"They face challenges in accessing capital","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"They always succeed more often than large companies","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-024","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["philosophy","ethics"],"passage":"The trolley problem, first introduced by philosopher Philippa Foot, has become one of the most famous thought experiments in moral philosophy. In its classic formulation, a runaway trolley is headed toward five people tied to the track, and the only way to save them is to pull a lever diverting the trolley to a different track where only one person is tied. Most people say they would pull the lever, endorsing a utilitarian calculation that saving five lives justifies sacrificing one. However, in a variation where saving the five requires physically pushing a large man off a bridge onto the track, most people say they would not do so. This disparity reveals that moral judgments are influenced not only by outcomes but also by factors such as physical contact, directness of action, and the distinction between doing harm and merely allowing harm to occur.","question":"Which of the following ideas are discussed in relation to the trolley problem?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Utilitarian calculation of saving more lives","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"The distinction between doing harm and allowing harm","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"The influence of physical contact on moral judgments","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"The trolley problem proves all ethics are meaningless","isCorrect":false},{"id":"e","text":"People respond differently to seemingly similar scenarios","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-025","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["media","social media"],"passage":"The rise of social media has transformed how information spreads in society, with both positive and negative consequences. On the positive side, social media platforms allow marginalized voices to be heard, facilitate the organization of social movements, and enable rapid dissemination of important information during emergencies. However, these same platforms have also been used to spread misinformation and disinformation at unprecedented speed and scale. The algorithmic curation of content, designed to maximize user engagement, can create echo chambers where individuals are exposed primarily to information that reinforces their existing beliefs. Researchers and policymakers are exploring various approaches to address these challenges, including content moderation, digital literacy education, and algorithmic transparency requirements.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are consequences of social media?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Amplification of marginalized voices","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Rapid spread of misinformation","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Creation of echo chambers through algorithmic curation","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Facilitation of social movement organization","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Social media has only negative effects on society","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-026","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["health","exercise"],"passage":"Strength training, also known as resistance training, involves exercises that use resistance to induce muscular contraction, which builds strength, anaerobic endurance, and muscle mass. Benefits of regular strength training include increased bone density, improved joint function, and a higher resting metabolic rate, which helps with weight management. Additionally, strength training has been shown to reduce symptoms of several chronic conditions, including arthritis, back pain, and type 2 diabetes. The American College of Sports Medicine recommends that adults engage in strength training exercises for all major muscle groups at least twice per week, with at least 48 hours between sessions that target the same muscles.","question":"Which of the following benefits of strength training are mentioned in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Increased bone density","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Improved joint function","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Higher resting metabolic rate","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Reduced symptoms of type 2 diabetes","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Complete cure for all chronic conditions","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-027","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["history","technology"],"passage":"The Industrial Revolution, which began in Britain in the late 18th century, fundamentally transformed manufacturing processes and had far-reaching effects on society. The development of steam power allowed factories to be located away from water sources for the first time, while mechanized textile production dramatically increased the speed and volume of fabric manufacturing. The revolution also spurred urbanization as workers migrated from rural areas to cities in search of factory employment, leading to the rapid growth of industrial centers such as Manchester and Birmingham. While the revolution generated unprecedented wealth, it also produced deplorable working conditions, including long hours, low wages, and the widespread use of child labor. These conditions eventually led to labor reforms and the emergence of the trade union movement.","question":"Which of the following are mentioned as effects of the Industrial Revolution?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Factories could be built away from water sources","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Rapid urbanization and growth of industrial cities","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Widespread use of child labor in factories","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Emergence of the trade union movement","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Working conditions were excellent from the start","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-028","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["science","chemistry"],"passage":"The periodic table is one of the most important organizing principles in chemistry, arranging all known chemical elements in a systematic way based on their atomic structure and properties. Elements are ordered by increasing atomic number, which corresponds to the number of protons in the nucleus. The table is structured so that elements with similar chemical properties appear in the same vertical column, known as a group. For example, the noble gases, which are all chemically inert under normal conditions, appear in Group 18. The periodic table has proven to be a powerful predictive tool, as it allowed scientists to predict the existence and properties of elements that had not yet been discovered when the table was first developed.","question":"Which of the following are true about the periodic table according to the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Elements are ordered by increasing atomic number","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Elements with similar properties appear in the same group","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Noble gases are in Group 18","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"It allowed prediction of undiscovered elements","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"It organizes elements based only on their color","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-029","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["literature","philosophy"],"passage":"George Orwell's novel Nineteen Eighty-Four presents a dystopian vision of a totalitarian society where the government, led by the figure of Big Brother, exercises complete control over its citizens. The regime maintains power through several mechanisms, including constant surveillance, manipulation of historical records, and the imposition of Newspeak, a controlled language designed to eliminate the vocabulary for dissent and independent thought. The concept of doublethink, the ability to hold two contradictory beliefs simultaneously and accept both, is presented as an essential skill for Party members. Orwell's novel introduced terms and concepts that have entered common usage to describe oppressive governmental practices, including the adjective 'Orwellian' itself. The novel remains widely read and discussed as a warning about the dangers of unchecked state power.","question":"According to the passage, which methods of control are used in the society of Nineteen Eighty-Four?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Constant surveillance of citizens","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Manipulation of historical records","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Imposition of a controlled language called Newspeak","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"The concept of doublethink","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Free and open democratic elections","isCorrect":false},{"id":"f","text":"The novel's terms have entered common usage","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-030","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["sociology","economics"],"passage":"Income inequality, the extent to which income is distributed unevenly among a population, has been rising in many developed countries since the 1980s. Economists have identified several contributing factors, including technological changes that favor highly skilled workers, the decline of labor unions, and globalization that has shifted manufacturing jobs to lower-cost countries. The consequences of high inequality extend beyond economics, affecting social cohesion, political stability, and intergenerational mobility. Children from low-income families face significant disadvantages in educational opportunities and health outcomes compared to their wealthier peers. Proposed policy responses include progressive taxation, increased investment in public education, and strengthening social safety nets.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are causes of rising income inequality?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Technological changes favoring skilled workers","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Decline of labor unions","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Globalization shifting jobs to lower-cost countries","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"All countries have identical income distributions","isCorrect":false},{"id":"e","text":"Inequality affects social cohesion and political stability","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-031","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["nature","biology"],"passage":"Bees are among the most important pollinators in both natural ecosystems and agricultural systems. They transfer pollen between flowers of the same species, enabling plants to produce fruits and seeds. Approximately one-third of the food consumed by humans depends on pollination, with bees responsible for the majority of this service. Beyond their agricultural value, bees produce honey, beeswax, and other commercially valuable products. However, bee populations in many parts of the world have been declining due to a combination of factors including habitat loss, pesticide exposure, disease, and climate change. This decline has prompted conservation efforts such as creating pollinator-friendly gardens and reducing pesticide use.","question":"Which of the following are mentioned in the passage about bees?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"They are responsible for most agricultural pollination","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"About one-third of human food depends on pollination","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Bee populations are declining due to multiple factors","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Habitat loss is a contributing factor to bee decline","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Pesticide exposure has no effect on bee populations","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-032","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["technology","ethics"],"passage":"Facial recognition technology has advanced rapidly in recent years, with artificial intelligence systems now capable of identifying individuals with high accuracy in real time from video footage. This technology has legitimate applications in areas such as law enforcement, where it can help identify suspects, and in personal device security, where it enables convenient user authentication. However, the widespread deployment of facial recognition raises significant privacy and civil liberties concerns. Unlike passwords or identification numbers, faces cannot be changed if compromised. Moreover, studies have shown that many facial recognition systems exhibit racial and gender bias, misidentifying women and people of color at higher rates than white men. These concerns have led several cities and jurisdictions to restrict or ban government use of facial recognition technology.","question":"Which of the following concerns about facial recognition are discussed in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Privacy and civil liberties concerns","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Faces cannot be changed if compromised","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Racial and gender bias in identification accuracy","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Some jurisdictions have restricted its use","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"The technology has no legitimate applications","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-033","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["education","child development"],"passage":"Early childhood education has been shown to have lasting positive effects on cognitive development, social skills, and future academic achievement. High-quality preschool programs provide structured learning environments where children develop foundational literacy and numeracy skills through play-based activities. Equally important, children learn to interact with peers, follow routines, and regulate their emotions in a group setting. Longitudinal studies have found that children who attend quality preschool programs are more likely to graduate from high school, attend college, and have higher earnings as adults. The benefits are especially pronounced for children from disadvantaged backgrounds, making early childhood education an important tool for promoting social equity.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are benefits of early childhood education?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Development of foundational literacy and numeracy skills","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Learning to interact with peers and follow routines","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Higher likelihood of high school graduation","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Benefits are especially pronounced for disadvantaged children","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Early education has no effect on adult earnings","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-034","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["science","physics"],"passage":"Einstein's theory of general relativity, published in 1915, fundamentally changed our understanding of gravity. Rather than describing gravity as a force between masses, as Newton had done, Einstein proposed that massive objects curve the fabric of spacetime itself, and that this curvature is what we perceive as gravity. One of the theory's most striking predictions is the existence of gravitational waves, ripples in spacetime caused by the acceleration of massive objects such as merging black holes. These waves were directly detected for the first time in 2015 by the LIGO observatory, exactly one hundred years after Einstein published his theory. General relativity also predicts the existence of black holes, regions where spacetime is curved so severely that not even light can escape. The theory has passed every experimental test to which it has been subjected.","question":"Which of the following are mentioned in the passage about general relativity?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It describes gravity as curvature of spacetime","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"It predicts the existence of gravitational waves","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Gravitational waves were first detected in 2015","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"It predicts the existence of black holes","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Einstein rejected the concept of gravity entirely","isCorrect":false},{"id":"f","text":"It has passed every experimental test so far","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-035","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["business","leadership"],"passage":"Transformational leadership is a style of leadership where leaders work with their teams to identify needed change, create a vision to guide the change through inspiration, and execute the change in tandem with committed group members. Research has identified four key components of transformational leadership: idealized influence, where leaders serve as role models; inspirational motivation, where leaders articulate a compelling vision; intellectual stimulation, where leaders encourage creativity and innovation; and individualized consideration, where leaders attend to the needs of each team member. Studies have consistently found that transformational leadership is associated with higher employee satisfaction, greater organizational commitment, and improved overall performance compared to purely transactional approaches that focus on rewards and punishments.","question":"Which of the following are identified as components of transformational leadership?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Idealized influence as role models","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Inspirational motivation with a compelling vision","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Intellectual stimulation encouraging creativity","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Individualized consideration for each team member","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Relying exclusively on punishment to motivate","isCorrect":false},{"id":"f","text":"Associated with higher employee satisfaction","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-036","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["health","mental health"],"passage":"Mindfulness is the practice of intentionally focusing one's attention on the present moment without judgment. Originating from Buddhist meditation traditions, mindfulness has been adapted into secular therapeutic techniques that are now widely used in clinical settings. Mindfulness-based stress reduction programs have been shown to effectively reduce symptoms of anxiety, depression, and chronic pain. The practice can be cultivated through formal meditation sessions or integrated into daily activities such as eating, walking, and even washing dishes. Regular mindfulness practice has been associated with measurable changes in brain regions involved in attention, emotion regulation, and self-awareness.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are true about mindfulness?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It involves focusing attention on the present moment","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"It originated from Buddhist meditation traditions","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"It can reduce symptoms of anxiety and depression","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"It is associated with measurable brain changes","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"It can only be practiced during formal meditation","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-037","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["history","ancient civilizations"],"passage":"Ancient Egypt was one of the world's earliest and longest-lasting civilizations, flourishing along the Nile River for more than three millennia. The Nile's predictable annual floods deposited fertile silt on the surrounding land, enabling the highly productive agriculture that sustained a complex hierarchical society. Egyptian civilization produced remarkable achievements in architecture, including the pyramids at Giza, which remained the tallest man-made structures for nearly four thousand years. They developed a sophisticated writing system using hieroglyphs, made advances in mathematics and medicine, and created an elaborate religious system centered on concepts of the afterlife. The civilization was ruled by pharaohs, who were considered divine intermediaries between the gods and the people.","question":"Which of the following achievements or characteristics of Ancient Egypt are mentioned in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Construction of the pyramids at Giza","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Development of hieroglyphic writing","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Advances in mathematics and medicine","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Pharaohs were considered divine intermediaries","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Egypt was the shortest-lived ancient civilization","isCorrect":false},{"id":"f","text":"The Nile's floods enabled productive agriculture","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-038","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["technology","privacy"],"passage":"Data encryption is a fundamental technology for protecting digital information from unauthorized access. It works by converting readable data, known as plaintext, into an unreadable format called ciphertext using mathematical algorithms and encryption keys. Only parties with the corresponding decryption key can restore the data to its original readable form. Encryption is essential for securing online banking, e-commerce transactions, email communications, and virtually all forms of sensitive digital activity. End-to-end encryption, a particularly secure approach, ensures that only the communicating users can read messages, preventing even the service provider from accessing the content. Law enforcement agencies have sometimes argued for backdoor access to encrypted communications, but security experts warn that such backdoors would inevitably weaken security for all users.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are true about encryption?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It converts readable data into an unreadable format","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"It is essential for securing online banking","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"End-to-end encryption prevents service providers from reading messages","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Security experts support backdoors for law enforcement","isCorrect":false},{"id":"e","text":"Only parties with the decryption key can restore data","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-039","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["politics","international law"],"passage":"The Geneva Conventions comprise a series of international treaties that establish standards of humanitarian treatment for victims of armed conflict. First adopted in 1864 and significantly expanded after World War II in 1949, the conventions protect wounded and sick soldiers, prisoners of war, and civilians in war zones. The conventions prohibit torture, degrading treatment, and attacks on medical personnel and facilities marked with the red cross or red crescent emblem. All 196 countries in the world have ratified the Geneva Conventions, making them universally applicable. However, compliance remains a persistent challenge, as violations continue to occur in conflicts around the world, and enforcement mechanisms are often weak or politically constrained.","question":"Which of the following statements about the Geneva Conventions are supported by the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"They were first adopted in 1864","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"They protect prisoners of war and civilians","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"They prohibit torture and degrading treatment","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"All 196 countries have ratified them","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Enforcement is always strictly applied without exception","isCorrect":false},{"id":"f","text":"Violations continue in conflicts despite universal ratification","isCorrect":true}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-040","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["environment","sustainability"],"passage":"Recycling is the process of converting waste materials into new products, thereby reducing the consumption of raw materials and energy while decreasing pollution. Commonly recycled materials include paper, glass, metal, plastic, and electronic waste. Recycling has significant environmental benefits, including reducing the amount of waste sent to landfills and incinerators, conserving natural resources such as timber and minerals, and lowering greenhouse gas emissions from manufacturing processes. However, the effectiveness of recycling programs depends on several factors, including public participation rates, the availability of recycling infrastructure, and the market demand for recycled materials. Contamination of recyclable materials with food waste or non-recyclable items remains a significant challenge for many municipal recycling programs.","question":"Which of the following benefits of recycling are mentioned in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Reducing waste sent to landfills","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Conserving natural resources","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Lowering greenhouse gas emissions","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Contamination is a significant challenge","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Recycling requires no public participation","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-041","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["psychology","cognition"],"passage":"Growth mindset, a concept developed by psychologist Carol Dweck, refers to the belief that intelligence and abilities can be developed through effort, learning, and persistence. This stands in contrast to a fixed mindset, where individuals believe their qualities are innate and unchangeable. Research has shown that students with a growth mindset tend to embrace challenges, persist in the face of setbacks, and see effort as a path to mastery. These attitudes contribute to higher academic achievement compared to students with a fixed mindset, who may avoid challenges for fear of failure. Importantly, mindsets themselves can be changed through targeted interventions, and teaching students about the malleability of the brain has been shown to improve academic outcomes, particularly for struggling students.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are true about growth mindset?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It was developed by psychologist Carol Dweck","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"It involves believing abilities can be developed through effort","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Students with growth mindset embrace challenges","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Mindsets can be changed through targeted interventions","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Growth mindset has no effect on academic achievement","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-042","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["science","medicine"],"passage":"The development of antibiotics in the 20th century transformed medicine by providing effective treatments for bacterial infections that had previously been major causes of death. Penicillin, discovered by Alexander Fleming in 1928, was the first true antibiotic, and its widespread use during World War II saved countless lives. In the decades that followed, many additional antibiotics were developed, dramatically reducing mortality from pneumonia, tuberculosis, and surgical infections. However, the overuse of antibiotics in both human medicine and agriculture has accelerated the evolution of antibiotic-resistant bacteria. The World Health Organization now considers antimicrobial resistance one of the top ten global public health threats, warning of a post-antibiotic era in which common infections could once again become deadly.","question":"Which of the following are mentioned in the passage about antibiotics?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Penicillin was discovered by Alexander Fleming in 1928","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Antibiotics saved lives during World War II","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Overuse has accelerated antibiotic resistance","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"WHO considers antimicrobial resistance a top health threat","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Bacteria never develop resistance to antibiotics","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-043","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["sports","health"],"passage":"Participating in team sports offers numerous benefits beyond physical fitness. Young people who play team sports learn valuable life skills including cooperation, communication, and how to work effectively with others toward shared goals. The experience of winning and losing helps develop emotional resilience and the ability to handle both success and disappointment gracefully. Regular sports participation is also associated with improved academic performance, as the discipline and time management skills developed through athletics transfer to academic settings. Additionally, team sports provide social connections and a sense of belonging that can protect against loneliness and depression, particularly during adolescence.","question":"Which of the following benefits of team sports are mentioned in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Learning cooperation and communication skills","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Developing emotional resilience through winning and losing","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Association with improved academic performance","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Providing social connections and a sense of belonging","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Team sports have no effect on mental health","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-044","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["literature","contemporary fiction"],"passage":"Magical realism is a literary genre in which fantastical elements are presented as a natural part of an otherwise realistic world. Originating in Latin American literature with writers such as Gabriel Garcia Marquez and Isabel Allende, the genre blends the extraordinary with the everyday in ways that challenge conventional distinctions between reality and imagination. In Marquez's landmark novel One Hundred Years of Solitude, for instance, a character ascends to heaven while folding sheets, and yellow butterflies precede a lover's appearance. These supernatural occurrences are narrated with the same matter-of-fact tone as mundane events, creating a narrative texture in which miracles and ordinary life coexist seamlessly. The genre often serves to express cultural identities, political critiques, and the legacy of colonialism in ways that purely realistic fiction cannot.","question":"Which of the following are characteristics of magical realism as described in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Fantastical elements presented as natural parts of everyday life","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Originated in Latin American literature","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Supernatural events narrated matter-of-factly","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Often expresses cultural identity and political critique","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Gabriel Garcia Marquez is associated with the genre","isCorrect":true},{"id":"f","text":"Fantastical elements are always explained scientifically","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-045","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["economics","development"],"passage":"Microfinance, the provision of small loans and other financial services to individuals who lack access to traditional banking, emerged as a popular development strategy in the 1990s. The model was pioneered by Muhammad Yunus and the Grameen Bank in Bangladesh, who demonstrated that poor individuals, particularly women, could be reliable borrowers when organized into small accountability groups. Microfinance was initially hailed as a powerful tool for poverty alleviation, with supporters arguing that it empowers individuals to start small businesses and invest in education and healthcare. However, more recent research has tempered these early expectations, finding that while microfinance can smooth consumption and help households manage financial shocks, its impact on long-term poverty reduction has been more modest than initially claimed. Concerns have also been raised about high interest rates and over-indebtedness among borrowers.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are true about microfinance?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It was pioneered by Muhammad Yunus and Grameen Bank","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"It provides financial services to those without traditional banking access","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Impact on long-term poverty reduction has been modest","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Concerns exist about high interest rates and over-indebtedness","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"It has completely eliminated poverty worldwide","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-046","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["food","cooking"],"passage":"Fermented foods have been part of human diets for thousands of years, with different cultures developing their own traditional fermented products. Common examples include yogurt, cheese, sauerkraut, kimchi, miso, and kombucha. The fermentation process not only preserves food but also enhances its nutritional value by increasing the bioavailability of certain vitamins and minerals. Many fermented foods contain live beneficial bacteria known as probiotics, which can support gut health by promoting a diverse and balanced intestinal microbiome. Emerging research suggests that a healthy gut microbiome may influence not only digestion but also immune function, mental health, and even body weight regulation. However, not all fermented foods contain live probiotics, as some are pasteurized or otherwise processed in ways that kill the beneficial microorganisms.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are benefits of fermented foods?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Preservation of food","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Enhanced nutritional value","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Supporting gut health through probiotics","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Potential influence on immune function and mental health","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"All fermented foods contain live probiotics","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-047","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["science","climate"],"passage":"The greenhouse effect is a natural process that warms the Earth's surface, making it habitable for life. When solar radiation reaches Earth's atmosphere, some of it is reflected back into space while the rest is absorbed and re-radiated as heat by greenhouse gases such as carbon dioxide, methane, and water vapor. Without this natural greenhouse effect, Earth's average surface temperature would be approximately minus 18 degrees Celsius rather than the current 15 degrees. However, human activities, primarily the burning of fossil fuels and deforestation, have dramatically increased the concentration of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere, amplifying the greenhouse effect and causing global temperatures to rise. This enhanced greenhouse effect is the primary driver of contemporary climate change.","question":"Which of the following statements about the greenhouse effect are supported by the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"It is a natural process that makes Earth habitable","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Greenhouse gases include carbon dioxide and methane","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Human activities have amplified the greenhouse effect","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Burning fossil fuels increases greenhouse gas concentrations","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"The greenhouse effect has no relationship to climate change","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-048","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":4,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["art","film history"],"passage":"German Expressionist cinema of the 1920s was characterized by highly stylized visuals, including distorted perspectives, exaggerated shadows, and theatrical acting that externalized characters' psychological states. Films such as The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari and Nosferatu used painted sets with angular, non-realistic geometry to create a sense of anxiety and unease. The movement emerged in the aftermath of World War I, reflecting the collective trauma and social dislocation of Weimar Germany. When the Nazi Party came to power in 1933, many German filmmakers emigrated to Hollywood, where they profoundly influenced the development of American film noir in the 1940s. The visual language of German Expressionism, with its emphasis on chiaroscuro lighting and psychological atmosphere, has continued to influence horror and thriller films to the present day.","question":"Which of the following are characteristics of German Expressionist cinema as described in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Highly stylized visuals with distorted perspectives","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Exaggerated shadows and theatrical acting","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Emergence in post-World War I Germany","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Influence on American film noir","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Continued influence on horror films today","isCorrect":true},{"id":"f","text":"Realistic sets with natural lighting","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-049","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":2,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["health","wellness"],"passage":"Hydration is essential for virtually every bodily function, from regulating body temperature to transporting nutrients and removing waste products. Water makes up approximately 60 percent of the adult human body, underscoring its fundamental importance. Dehydration, even at mild levels of just one to two percent body water loss, can impair cognitive performance, reduce physical endurance, and negatively affect mood. While the traditional recommendation of eight glasses of water per day serves as a useful guideline, individual water needs vary based on factors such as body size, activity level, climate, and overall diet. Foods with high water content, such as fruits and vegetables, also contribute to total fluid intake. The most reliable indicator of adequate hydration is urine color, with pale yellow generally indicating proper hydration.","question":"According to the passage, which of the following are true about hydration?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Water makes up about 60 percent of the adult body","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Mild dehydration can impair cognitive performance","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Individual water needs vary based on activity and climate","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Foods with high water content contribute to fluid intake","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"Everyone needs exactly eight glasses of water daily","isCorrect":false}]},{"id":"MCMA-R-050","type":"MCMA-R","skill":"reading","difficulty":3,"timeLimit":180,"instructions":"阅读文章并选择所有正确答案。","tags":["technology","innovation"],"passage":"3D printing, also known as additive manufacturing, builds three-dimensional objects by depositing material layer by layer based on a digital model. This technology offers several advantages over traditional subtractive manufacturing methods, which cut away material from a solid block. 3D printing produces less waste, enables the creation of complex geometries that would be impossible with conventional techniques, and allows for rapid prototyping without expensive tooling. In medicine, 3D printing is being used to create customized prosthetics, dental implants, and even tissue scaffolds for regenerative medicine. The construction industry has begun experimenting with 3D-printed buildings, with some companies claiming significant reductions in construction time and labor costs. Despite its promise, limitations remain including relatively slow production speeds, material constraints, and the need for post-processing of printed parts.","question":"Which of the following advantages or applications of 3D printing are mentioned in the passage?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Less waste compared to traditional manufacturing","isCorrect":true},{"id":"b","text":"Enables complex geometries not possible conventionally","isCorrect":true},{"id":"c","text":"Used for customized prosthetics and dental implants","isCorrect":true},{"id":"d","text":"Construction of buildings with reduced time and labor","isCorrect":true},{"id":"e","text":"3D printing has no limitations whatsoever","isCorrect":false}]}]`);export{e as default};